open workspace
    Prefill the editor with a Smalltalk counter example.
    Create Counter, increment twice, add ten, and read its value: twelve.
open object inspector
    Request current object inspection.
    Display placement, mailbox depth, root path and unavailable-reference context.
    Display active calls and outbound waits with their targets and chain identifiers.
    Preserve variable and method lists; wrap long diagnostic text.
close inspector
    Dismiss when Escape is pressed or the backdrop is clicked.
header
    Display the Ctrl+Enter shortcut.
retention display
    Omit the explanatory retention note.
interactive inspector
    Select or type a method and enter typed arguments.
    Send through MCP call, display result or error, refresh object fields.
    Follow object references in fields and results to their inspectors.
    Show only Class and ID in Live Objects.
method buttons
    Sort selectors alphabetically before rendering.
    Unary button clicks invoke immediately; other methods prepare arguments.
    Ignore method clicks while a call is pending.
